<h3><span>SPaG</span></h3>
<blockquote>
<p>On 28 August 1903, Foundation personnel educated in astrology sighted SCP-XXXX through a telescope near the Orion Arm.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This suggests that the telescope was situated in the Orion's Arm spiral arm, rather than the object was located in that sector. Additionally, &quot;astrology&quot; is defined by Merriam-Webster as &quot;the divination of the supposed influences of the stars and planets on human affairs and terrestrial events by their positions and aspects&quot;. I believe the word you are looking for is &quot;astronomy&quot;.</p>
<p>&quot;sighted&quot; is also defined as &quot;able to see : not blind.&quot; Perhaps &quot;observed&quot;.</p>
<hr />
<h3><span>Consistency/Flow</span></h3>
<blockquote>
<p>All deep-space observatories are to be monitored by satellite following standard procedure.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This could be cleaned up a bit to be more specific. It is unclear which standard procedure is being followed. Furthermore, I would assume that <span style="text-decoration: underline;">all</span> deep space observations would be closely monitored by the SCPF as a matter of course.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>The production and trade of new telescope parts such as refractors have been limited to companies where a sufficient number of undercover Foundation personnel are present.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This is also jumbled and unclear. What is this meant to prevent?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>All images of SCP-XXXX are to be intercepted by the Foundation AI &quot;Binary star&quot;, saved in the Foundation database, and subsequently deleted from public records.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I have a personal preference for utilizing the .aic convention. In this case, your AI would become Binary_Star.aic. I think it looks cleaner than &quot;name&quot;, in that it specifies an entity rather than a &quot;supposed&quot; entity. It's all in the implication.</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-XXXX is the first spacecraft ever observed by the Foundation.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Non-human or non-terrestrial? Or did this observation predate Sputnik and the other Earth-based spacecraft?</p>
<hr />
<h3><span>Closing Remarks</span></h3>
<p>There are significant errors throughout this piece, what is represented here are just a few examples. The idea is a sound one and I think the additional story told throughout the listpages is interesting. However, there are a lot of sentence structure and word choice errors that make this difficult to read.</p>
<p>Ping me on IRC at your leisure and we can go over more of them if you'd like.</p>
</div>
